<article class="env-definition" id="020H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/020H">Definition <span data-tag="020H">33.9.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme over the field $k$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $x \in X$. We say $X$ is <em>geometrically pointwise integral at $x$</em> if for every field extension $k'/k$ and every $x' \in X_{k'}$ lying over $x$ the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X_{k'}, x'}$ is integral. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $X$ is <em>geometrically pointwise integral</em> if $X$ is geometrically pointwise integral at every point. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $X$ is <em>geometrically integral</em> over $k$ if the scheme $X_{k'}$ is integral for every field extension $k'$ of $k$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>